      0x7ad00  A_L2L1_0_0_cons_buff_0
      0x7bd00  A_L2L1_0_0_cons_buff_1
    bank 3: EMPTY
  (16 core ELFs in this build; the first is shown, and the allocation is per core)

BANK SHARING
  bank 2 holds 2 distinct buffers: A_L2L1_0_0_cons, B_L2L1_0_0_cons
  banks with nothing in them: [3]

BUNDLES THAT ISSUE TWO LOADS
  .text.matmul_i8_i32: 10 of 144 bundles
    loop .L_LEnd0: 1 of 9 bundles  <-- in the steady-state loop
      0x0200  vlda	wl3, [p4], #0x20 | vldb	wl8, [p3], #0x20 | vmov	x0, x4 | vmac	cm3, cm3, x10, x9, r4

VERDICT
  HAZARD. 1 paired-load bundle(s) inside hardware loops, and
  a bank holds more than one buffer. If a paired load reads two buffers in
  the same bank it costs one extra cycle per iteration, so a loop's bundle
  count understates its cycles by that much.
  Bank(s) [3] are empty, so the collision is avoidable.

